sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Dactylioceras commune Turing k_c at 24 µm (pass 1, stage 1) faithfully reproduces Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: datasets/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0/pass1_growth.gif; organism: Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-inhibitor kinetics a - u + u^2 v, b - u^2 v. | Catalogue slot: 24 µm detail scale, SI size 2.419e-05 m, Toarcian 181 Ma, D_f = 1.55. | James St. John, CC BY 2.0: Whitby Formation Dactylioceras commune, stated width 57 mm.; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv solved so k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv) returns 2.419e-05 m. | Stage-1 synthetic fibulate coil used only as a first visual check.; transfer_boundary: Molluscan aperture pigment models are the transfer path onto an ammonite periostracum. Pass 1 does not test that transfer against the photograph.; does_not_claim: Pass 1 does not claim a dispersion-curve Pearson r, an ablation, a parameter sweep, or a rib measurement. | Pass 1 does not claim that 24 µm stripes are visible on the 57 mm shell. | D_f = 1.55 is a catalogue input, not a measurement on this photograph.]; other sources: Dactylioceras commune ammonite fossil from Yorkshire, England <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dactylioceras_commune_Ammonite_Fossil_from_Yorkshire_England.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 30 µm (2.99e-05 m, log10=-4.524 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 30 µm to 6.7 cm): 30 µm:dactylioceras-commune-bioelectric-polarity, 93 µm:dactylioceras-commune-vertex-packing, 1.5 mm:dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength, 3.0 mm:dactylioceras-commune-clock-wavefront, 6.7 mm:dactylioceras-commune-morphogen-condensation, 8.2 mm:dactylioceras-commune-elastic-buckling, 9.3 mm:dactylioceras-commune-flux-canalization, 1.3 cm:dactylioceras-commune-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0094837300010046>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0094837300013336>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1145/142920.134096> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

